Plan is to translate the python program into a functionally identical, but
vastly more efficient and cool, C program.

By 'the python program' I mean my other encoder that is written in python which
is in a different repository.

---

Not yet workable:

- Can't cope with very long words or very large texts (just on account of
  allocating though).
- Haven't yet done that thing about prioritising certain word lengths and
  ensuring maximal byte savings.
- If a word is all caps, or has any other curious sort of structure, it would
  just have all its personality wiped away I imagine.
- Multi-word symbols or number-based symbols aren't part of it.
- No decoder yet obviously lol. Should be doable in a single loop though so
  that's neat.
